<title>UK: Yugoslav debt talks said to end, new talks in July.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav debt talks said to end, new talks in July.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslavia has adjourned talks with its commerical bank creditors in London to restructure $2.4 billion of debt but new talks are scheduled to resume in July, a source close to the negotiations said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Further economic and financial information will be presented at a joint meeting in July,&quot; said the source.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Diane Craft, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5110</p>
